# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored; this file is not.
#
# The app needs two variables. Without SESSION_SECRET, signing in throws a
# server error. Without DATABASE_URL, nothing loads at all.

# Signs the session cookie. Must be at least 32 characters, and must be the
# same value everywhere a given set of cookies has to stay valid: change it and
# every signed-in user is signed out, because their cookie no longer verifies.
#
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
#
# On Vercel this goes in Settings > Environment Variables, applied to
# Production, Preview and Development.
SESSION_SECRET=replace-me-with-at-least-32-random-characters

# The Postgres connection string. Ours is a free Neon database — no card, no
# server to run. Copy it from the Neon dashboard: your project > Connect.
#
# The line below is a PLACEHOLDER. Every REPLACE-ME has to go, including the
# one in the host name. A real Neon host looks like
# `ep-some-words-1a2b3c4d-pooler.c-5.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech` — long, with
# a random-looking middle. If you ever see REPLACE-ME in an error message, the
# placeholder was copied somewhere by mistake.
#
# When pasting into Vercel, paste the VALUE only: start at `postgresql://`,
# stop at `require`. Leave out the `DATABASE_URL=` and both quote marks. The
# quotes belong to this file's format; Vercel has no format, so whatever you
# paste becomes the value, quote marks and all.
#
# Keep `sslmode=verify-full`. It tells the driver to check the database's
# certificate properly, which is what stops someone impersonating the server.
# Neon's own copy button writes `sslmode=require`, which is weaker.
#
# This is a PASSWORD. It belongs in .env and in Vercel's environment
# variables, and nowhere else — not in a commit, not in a chat message. If it
# ever does end up somewhere public, reset the role password in Neon
# (Dashboard > Roles) and put the new string here; the old one dies instantly.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://REPLACE-ME:REPLACE-ME@REPLACE-ME.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=verify-full&channel_binding=require"
